<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Polish crown</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, also known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-the-kingdom-of-poland">Crown of the Kingdom of Poland</a>, was the Polish state that entered a union with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. After a long personal union under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty">Jagiellonian dynasty</a>, the two were joined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> in 1569. This created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Poland" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Tora or Alex K in Ukranian and Japanese wiki · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Poland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
